.ac-pc-key i.spent { border:1.5px solid var(--dgm-line); }
.ac-pc-key i.kept { background:linear-gradient(90deg, var(--blue-hi) 50%, var(--teal-dk) 50%); }
[data-theme="light"] .ac-pc-key i.kept { background:linear-gradient(90deg, var(--blue) 50%, var(--teal-dk) 50%); }

/* WHERE THE MONEY MOVES: amber where it costs more, gray where it costs less. 2026-09-22.
   It was red and green, and in the Chart view that green sat directly under Utah's teal bar:
   normal-vision Delta E 5.0 between them, so "costs less" and "the place you are going" were
   the same colour meaning two different things. Amber is the tool's one colour for "worse for
   you" everywhere else (the answer, the summary, the pay-runs-out line), so it now means that
