  <div class="shell-foot">
    <span class="ac-foot-note">Every number here is an estimate. Not tax, legal, or financial advice.</span>
    {% set ta_source = 'MERIC COL Q1 2026 · GSA per diem · 2025 state tax tables' %}
    {% include "components/tool-attribution.njk" %}
    <span class="ac-foot-year" id="acFootYear"></span>
  </div>

  <div class="shell-sheet" id="acMethodSheet" role="dialog" aria-modal="false" aria-label="Methodology and sources">
    <button class="icon-btn hu-sheet-x" id="acMethodClose" aria-label="Close"><i data-lucide="x"></i></button>
    <div class="ac-method">
      <h2>How this works</h2>
      <p>You enter what you actually pay each month. The tool scales each category by the ratio between the two states' cost indexes, computes state income tax from the real 2025 bracket tables (plus mandatory payroll deductions like CA SDI and WA Cares), subtracts federal tax and FICA on each side, and compares what is left over each month. By default the same gross rides both columns; enter the offer's own pay and each column uses its own gross with its own tax math. The breakeven number inverts the comparison: the gross pay the assignment location needs before you are trading down.</p>
      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Housing, county grain: <a href="https://www.zillow.com/research/data/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Zillow ZORI</a> market rents where covered, <a href="https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Census ACS 5-year</a> median rents everywhere else. County profile stats (income, home value, commute, property tax) are ACS + ZHVI.</li>
        <li>All other cost ratios: <a href="https://meric.mo.gov/data/cost-living-data-series" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MERIC Cost of Living Index</a>, state grain. Insurance has no MERIC category; it scales by the miscellaneous index as a stand-in.</li>
        <li>State tax: 2025 bracket tables from state revenue departments and the Tax Foundation. Payroll programs (SDI, PFML, TDI) included where they take real money. Sales tax figures: Tax Foundation combined state and average local.</li>
        <li>Insurance risk flags: <a href="https://hazards.fema.gov/nri/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FEMA National Risk Index</a>, counties rated Very High or Relatively High for wildfire, flood, quake, hurricane, tornado, or hail.</li>
        <li>Per diem: <a href="https://www.gsa.gov/travel/plan-book/per-diem-rates" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GSA per diem rates</a>, live by county for the current federal fiscal year.</li>
        <li>License logistics: compact membership verified against the compact commissions (<a href="https://www.nursecompact.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NLC</a>, <a href="https://ptcompact.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PT Compact</a>, <a href="https://www.imlcc.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">IMLC</a>, <a href="https://psypact.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PSYPACT</a>, <a href="https://respiratorycarecompact.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RCIC</a>). RCIC status is maintained by hand here; the author chairs the USRC Legislative Affairs Committee and has a professional stake in keeping it current. Fees and timelines are planning approximations.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What it does not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Local income taxes (Maryland counties, Ohio cities, PA municipalities, NYC, Indiana counties) are FLAGGED, not computed. Where they apply they are material.</li>
        <li>Stipend taxability, tax-home rules, and multistate filing are real topics this tool does not touch. Talk to a tax professional who knows travel contracts.</li>
        <li>Hourly pay annualizes at 52 weeks times weekly hours on both sides. A 13-week contract is not a year; the comparison holds because both columns share the convention, but the annual figures are conventions, not predictions.</li>
        <li>County rents fix the worst of the state-average blur, but only for housing. Groceries, transportation, and the rest are still state ratios, and a county is still not a zip code. The Assumptions panel exists so you can correct for what you know.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="vh" aria-live="polite" id="acLive"></div>
</div>

